    {
      "id": "claim_a1a35dbe722dee15ca61262831753a6ffe716808b63c67a20518646b5dd77063",
      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Transience implies ballisticity for uniformly elliptic i.i.d. RWRE (open, d >= 2) is a statement about the first moment of the regeneration time, and the polynomial condition (P)_M is a moment self-improvement",
      "body": "PRIVATE REDUCTION, author-recorded. Under (IID)+(UE) transience in direction l gives the Sznitman-Zerner regeneration structure with tau_1 < infinity a.s.; ballisticity is E[tau_1 | D = infinity] < infinity (Drewitz-Ramirez Open Question 2.20). Under (UE) a trap of diameter r holds the walk at most exponentially long in r, so sub-ballistic behaviour needs polynomially rare traps of logarithmic size along the path, which i.i.d. environments do allow; the question is whether the tail P(tau_1 > n) can be as heavy as n^{-1+eps}. Open Question 3.20 (does positive velocity imply (P)_M for M > 15d + 5) is then the question whether a finite first moment of tau_1 self-improves to moments of order about M/d, because (P)_M is equivalent through the slab decomposition to high moments of tau_1. The Guerra-Ramirez theorem (T) <=> (T') (2018) settles Open Question 3.28 but neither of these. Recorded as the moment-self-improvement reformulation.\nRandom walk in i.i.d. uniformly elliptic environment on Z^d, d >= 2\nRegeneration structure of Sznitman-Zerner",
      "metadata": {
        "artifact_digest": "sha256:48e51ef4a076ceb10a2ab8135e088d6487a3298024f1a6e22583200ad3c9b866",
        "artifact_path": "objects/sha256/48/48e51ef4a076ceb10a2ab8135e088d6487a3298024f1a6e22583200ad3c9b866.md",
