      "title": "Open problem: Transience in a direction implies ballisticity for uniformly elliptic i.i.d. RWRE in d >= 2",
      "body": "OPEN PROBLEM (source_says_open; current status no_resolution_found_in_documented_search; result status attempted_unsolved). Let d >= 2 and the RWRE satisfy (UE) and (IID) and be transient in direction l. Is the walk necessarily ballistic in direction l? Source: Drewitz and Ramirez: Selected topics in random walks in random environment, Open question 2.20, p. 24. Status notes: Bounded search 2026-09-07: Guerra and Ramirez (arXiv 1809.02011, 'A proof of Sznitman's conjecture about ballistic RWRE') proved the equivalence of conditions (T) and (T'), which is Open question 3.28 of the source, NOT this question; no proof that transience implies ballisticity in d >= 2 was found.\nPosed in Drewitz and Ramirez: Selected topics in random walks in random environment\nCurrent status no_resolution_found_in_documented_search as of 2026-09-07",
